      "content": "Yeah, all of our employees have were pretty extensive hiring process as far as personnel they're all full-time. Employees if they are part time it just means they're going to Clos school or have a second job but everyone's an Eside employee we don't have contract work or day labors they all go through a phone interview in person interview trial base. Where they actually get tested in the field on moves to see if they have what it takes. See if they culture fits and then as far as insurance that's included in the hourly rates and we go well above, beyond every other company, most moving companies supply the 60\u00a2 per pound per article coverage which is based on the way the item and pretty minimal we have our no worries damage covers which is up to $2,000 evaluation coverage per move to repair replace or provide a cast summit for any item damage during the move even if the guys are moving things on site depending on the item they generally if we're moving things from one location to the next we're generally.",
